Started off as normal really, no different from any other game except
for one thing.  This time it was personnal.  I've been playing on and
off for a couple of years now and a few weeks a go I saw the medusas
isle for the first time.  I know. I think I play too fast.  Anywho, I
been concentrating real good like since then.  The game before this I
was in the castle and I died thanks to a master mind-flayer (killed by
brainlessness, how embarassing!)  So this time, I was determined to
make it further.

Went down the mines first, down to the shop level, the alter wasn't
aligned to Tyr so blurgh.  Robbed a couple of shops with my pet and
bought some protection.   With a dwarvish mithril coat, and helmet my
AC was pretty good.  Went back up then down main dungeon, completed
sokoban to find a bag of holding. Yay! I say "Yay!" because I'd
already found an amulet of Reflection in a shop and nicked it.

Back up to the mines, bit more protection, think I polypiled a bit and
got some speed boots and a t-shirt.  And I found a +3 crystal plate
mail. But i decided that the weight was too much, I stuck with my
dwarvish mail.   Down down down to the bottom of the mines, Got a
luckstone, dipped for excalibar, went back up then down to medusas
isle.  At this point I had not found one alter in the main dungeon.  A
litle hash I feel.  So i went back the mines and converted the alter
there, butchering the priest in the process.  Got all my money back
tho!   Blessed, my luckstone and boH.  Then I polyed some scrolls and
enchanted armour. Think my AC was about -20 by the time I left.

Did the quest.  Easy.

Killed medusa, no problem with the AoR, then down to the castle.  Had
a ring of regeneration and conflict (and levitation) so pretty much
everyone wiped everyone else out, and I cleaned up the rest.  My
Excalibar was +6 so woot.

