To go to Hell!

Gehennon was actually fairly easy, if a little tense.  The demons were
no problem I just battered them untill they submitted.  Vlad was easy
too, except that about three monsters all read scrolls of create
monster and the tower was filled with dragons and titans and stuff.
Found the vibrating square then went to kill Rodney.  I zapped him
with a wand of death I found after he went all double trouble on me,
got the book then went and performed the incantation.

The high priest was a bit nasty, plus there was a bucketfull of big
assed monsters there.  Eventually he submitted and I got the amulet
and ran for it.

Up one level down two. Rodney was a constant pain in my side as he
apeared on just about every level.  Eventually he stole the amulet
from me and I chased him up the stairs the stood on the last staircase
pf hell and hit him untill he died (again).  I also lost Mjollnir as I
threw it at a green slime, then got trapped and had to use a wand of
teleport to zap it away from me.  Rodney kept creating monsters and I
had to just force my way through on levels with no teleport allowed. I
only zapped him with the wand of death twice I think, the rest was all
melee combat kills.

I had teleport and tele control as intrisics so I moved pretty fast up
through the dungeon, rodney apeared a few more times but I saw him off
with my +5 excalibar.

The plane of earth was fun.  Rodney got confused by an umber hulk
thanks to my ring of conflict and mas produced acid blobs.  The portal
was in the first cave I got to.  On the plane of Air I just slipped on
my ring of levitation and ran for it.  The plane of fire was quite
hard just because it took me ages to find the portal, and Rodney was
back again (for the last time).  The plane of water was real easy
because I'd genocided Krakens and Giant eels.

So finally the Astral plane.  Third time lucky.  I just waded through
the nasties and finally made it to the right alter, I was wearing two
rings of regenaration now so I don't think much could threaten me.
Found the alter and sacrificed the amulet.

